                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bb1afdf8-e2aa-3fe0-9112-effec60b763a",
                        "entry_id": "8d318a37-f392-3d97-ae45-4b05572b9c44",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Variété d’orange (Citrus sinensis cv. Navel)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2bf08707-9b21-4190-87ca-0689cedbb328",
                                "sense_id": "bb1afdf8-e2aa-3fe0-9112-effec60b763a",
                                "text": "La navel, avec sa forme caractéristique en « nombril », est idéale à dévorer nature ou dans les desserts."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d472c87a-3b39-435e-bd20-6125b7c51ba5",
                                "sense_id": "bb1afdf8-e2aa-3fe0-9112-effec60b763a",
                                "text": "Les navels ou « oranges à nombril », sans pépins, sont reconnaissables à l’espèce d’ombilic qui marque l’un des pôles du fruit. — (Gontier Josette, L’oranger, 95 p., page 25, 2000, Actes Sud, Le nom de l’arbre)"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d0f625be-ca7d-444c-bb12-3e5316a26c65",
                        "source_entry_id": "8d318a37-f392-3d97-ae45-4b05572b9c44",
                        "source_sense_id": "bb1afdf8-e2aa-3fe0-9112-effec60b763a",
                        "target_lang_word": "navel",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "navel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fc9816ad-4a62-3042-b5b0-6ca52a5b25de",
                                        "entry_id": "f8141e2c-45ac-3d48-bbd9-0f2a381c6dc8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The indentation or bump remaining in the abdomen of placental mammals where the umbilical cord was attached before birth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6f897984-1a69-32f7-a94c-3578124ea756",
                                        "entry_id": "f8141e2c-45ac-3d48-bbd9-0f2a381c6dc8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The central part or point of anything; the middle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ce5f6c2-64aa-4f90-aec7-f87082d6f709",
                                                "sense_id": "6f897984-1a69-32f7-a94c-3578124ea756",
                                                "text": "Within the navel of this hideous wood,\nImmured in cypress shades, a sorcerer dwells,\nOf Bacchus and Circe born, great Comus"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04ed0615-a4c9-4a05-bddb-5be85e044525",
                                                "sense_id": "6f897984-1a69-32f7-a94c-3578124ea756",
                                                "text": "Sweeter than the muſk of Tatar, the morning breeze from the navel of every flower raviſhed perfume."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80b266f9-792d-49d8-92c6-dd6d25a9c3ea",
                                                "sense_id": "6f897984-1a69-32f7-a94c-3578124ea756",
                                                "text": "We sat alfresco on the edge of a “square,” in reality a pond of cobbly mud with a plinth plonked in its navel […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5148473a-4f68-3298-aa45-0220f9aee894",
                                        "entry_id": "f8141e2c-45ac-3d48-bbd9-0f2a381c6dc8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A navel orange."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "096139ec-9818-4dd9-a09c-dcfd51e2d5b5",
                                                "sense_id": "5148473a-4f68-3298-aa45-0220f9aee894",
                                                "text": "This contributed to a rapid rise in planted acreage in northern California, especially in navels, which are more suited to growing conditions there."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "23ed63da-89a6-32b1-ab03-fa39ff16bc82",
                                        "entry_id": "f8141e2c-45ac-3d48-bbd9-0f2a381c6dc8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An eye on the underside of a carronade for securing it to a carriage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "navel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "781abaa5-a407-3d84-9579-72f30938b5f7",
                                        "entry_id": "bc0966e9-ec2d-30f9-9731-52bb4e1b5443",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be in the middle of a landscape."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary",
                                            "poetic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41e558a7-768c-4a8a-98f8-be81e5f4faf9",
                                                "sense_id": "781abaa5-a407-3d84-9579-72f30938b5f7",
                                                "text": "Lo, Nemi! navelled in the woody hills / So far, that the uprooting wind which tears / The oak from his foundation, and which spills / The ocean o’er its boundary, and bears / Its foam against the skies, reluctant spares / The oval mirror of thy glassy lake; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27d15f44-c72b-40b0-ac6b-be784ac85bf4",
                                                "sense_id": "781abaa5-a407-3d84-9579-72f30938b5f7",
                                                "text": "Within the shade a ruined temple stands / To sight conspicuous, navelled in the pines, / Speaking of Grecian art, since Vandal hands / Defaced her structures, and despoiled her shrines."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "39203215-d6c7-45b0-abe6-28fa8744c719",
                                                "sense_id": "781abaa5-a407-3d84-9579-72f30938b5f7",
                                                "text": "I rejoice as I call back those pleasant times, when in the casement of our seminary, I rested my telescope on my shut-up Virgil, and looked off among the far-off hills in the lap of which the edifice was naveled, and saw the pretty girls of the farm-houses, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7889645-f95e-4c2b-b4ef-691ad52eaa6a",
                                                "sense_id": "781abaa5-a407-3d84-9579-72f30938b5f7",
                                                "text": "The crimson berry tree navelled upon this court / Twinkles a coded message, a wind-sun tingling chord, / Curious round her foot saunters one blue jay: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
